WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.680
Every once in a while, you get a craving that you&nbsp;
simply can't control: You absolutely, positively&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:10.560
need to watch a number of Batman movies. If you&nbsp;
feel like having a Batman movie marathon right now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:15.200
and don't have the time or inclination to track&nbsp;
down a bunch of bat-movies from different sources,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:20.080
then Netflix is your friend. The streaming&nbsp;
service carries a nice variety of Batman films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:24.240
and they're different enough that you won't ever&nbsp;
get bored. In fact, you'll be able to enjoy a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:28.880
whole bunch of different takes on both the Caped&nbsp;
Crusader himself as well as his rogues gallery,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:32.880
from Academy Award-winning efforts to&nbsp;
delightfully goofy animated creations.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:39.397
"OMG it's Batman. Batman."

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:43.360
What's up to you is not only which&nbsp;
of these titles you decide to watch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:45.520
but the order in which you choose to view them.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:49.840
Thankfully, we've got some ideas about how to&nbsp;
pull off a Gotham City-themed movie marathon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:54.880
with style, but first, here's every Batman&nbsp;
movie you can binge-watch on Netflix right now.

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:59.680
There are currently four Batman films on Netflix,&nbsp;
which is scientifically the optimal number for a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:03.920
proper movie marathon. In case that isn't&nbsp;
exciting enough, two of the Batman movies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:08.400
present on the streaming service right now are&nbsp;
"Batman Begins" and "The Dark Knight," the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:12.160
two installments in director Christopher&nbsp;
Nolan's acclaimed "Dark Knight" trilogy.

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:16.480
Together, the pair of live-action Batman movies&nbsp;
give you the chance to spend a good few hours with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:21.760
Christian Bale's grounded, growly version of the&nbsp;
Bat. In addition to Bale's version of Bruce Wayne,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:26.736
"Batman Begins" and "The Dark Knight" also feature&nbsp;
several truly memorable takes on some of the Caped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.736 --> 00:01:32.560
Crusader's most iconic villains, including Liam&nbsp;
Neeson's Ra's al Ghul, Cillian Murphy's Scarecrow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:37.360
Aaron Eckhart's Harvey Dent AKA Two-Face,&nbsp;
and, of course, Heath Ledger's Joker.

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:43.120
"You look nervous. Is it the scars?&nbsp;
You want to know how I got them?"

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:47.360
The supporting casts of both&nbsp;
films are also undeniably stellar,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:52.320
with reliable heavy hitters like Gary Oldman,&nbsp;
Michael Caine, Tom Wilkinson, and Morgan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:57.600
Freeman all showing up at various points as&nbsp;
important and notable DC Comics characters.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:02.880
Unfortunately, the third installment in Nolan's&nbsp;
Batman trilogy, 2012's "The Dark Knight Rises," is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:07.520
not on Netflix right now. If you're set on sitting&nbsp;
down and marathoning the entire Dark Knight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:12.320
trilogy, that means you'll have to look elsewhere&nbsp;
to watch its final chapter. The good news is that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:16.560
even without "The Dark Knight Rises," both&nbsp;
"Batman Begins" and "The Dark Knight" offer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:21.200
more than enough of the thrills necessary to make&nbsp;
one Netflix streaming session feel worthwhile.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:25.760
There are two other Batman movies available&nbsp;
to stream on Netflix right now: "Batman: The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:31.600
Killing Joke" and the 22-minute "LEGO DC Comics:&nbsp;
Batman Be-Leaguered." The former title pits Kevin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:36.640
Conroy's Batman against Mark Hamill's Joker in&nbsp;
an adaptation of Alan Moore and Brian Bolland's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:41.120
classic graphic novel. "Batman Be-Leaguered,"&nbsp;
meanwhile, sees a Troy Baker-voiced LEGO&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:46.480
Batman and the nascent Justice League embark on a&nbsp;
global battle against a truly surprising villain.

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:49.600
The two animated titles could not&nbsp;
be more different from each other,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:54.880
or from the Christopher Nolan-directed live-action&nbsp;
films that Netflix also has to offer. Fortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:59.680
that means there's room for you to toss some real&nbsp;
variety into your Batman-centric streaming plans.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:03.520
Depending on how you want to approach your&nbsp;
bat-marathon, you could start with something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:08.720
serious like "Batman Begins," and then follow that&nbsp;
film up with its actual sequel, "The Dark Knight."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:12.320
From there, you could let Heath Ledger's&nbsp;
fan-favorite Joker act as your gateway to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:17.280
true chaos as you slide from the comparatively&nbsp;
realistic Nolan-verse to the even darker world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:21.920
and more sinister plot of "The Killing Joke."&nbsp;
Finally, as you're winding down from the non-stop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:25.600
chaos of "The Killing Joke" and "The Dark&nbsp;
Knight," there's no better way to step out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:31.840
of the darkness of those films and back into the&nbsp;
light than by turning on "Batman Be-Leaguered."

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:37.120
"Ugh, I lose more Batsubs this way."

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:42.880
Alternatively, you could start soft and go from&nbsp;
"Batman: Be-Leaguered" to "Killing Joke" and end&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:47.600
with "Batman Begins" and "The Dark Knight," or&nbsp;
even sandwich the animated films in between the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:52.640
two Nolan movies. After all, it's your movie&nbsp;
marathon. There are no rules — there's only...

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:56.240
"The Bat Man."

